,************************************************************    EXTRA CHARGES   ***************************************************************
,**Here you can set extra charges to your price list. The first 5 are charges that are taxed, the 2nd group of 5 are
,** not taxed. If you do not do tax, then it won't matter which group you use.
,**
,**The first question should be set to yes, this turns on the charge. The next question determines whether the
,** charge will be added the total or subtracted from the total. The next question is what will print on the subtotal line.
,**
,**From there you have 7 questions that determine how the charge is figured. Think of these questions as
,**3 pairs +1. The first pair works off of dollar totals. The options are SubTotal, SubTotal before extras, SubTotal of
,**Cabinets, SubTotal of Doors, SubTotal of Drawer Boxes, SubTotal of Pullouts.
,**
,**Subtotal is the current subtotal having added everything together right up to this extra charge.
,**Subtotal before extras the price of all the itemized units, those that would be listed in the contract report. It will
,**not include handles hinges, doors and drawer boxes (if listed separately).
,**Subtotal of cabinets includes the total price of cabinets only (no panels, valances etc) NOT including doors,
,**drawers or other extras.
,**SubTotal of Doors is the total cost of doors and drawer fronts in the job
,**SubTotal of Drawer Boxes is the total cost of Drawer Boxes in the job
,**SubTotal of Pullouts is the total cost of Pullouts in the job.
,**
,**Select one of these and then set an amount that total will be multiplied by. If you set the amount to zero it will
,**have no effect.
,**
,**Next Pair deals with lengths. Lineal, Square or Cubic foot amounts.
,**Lineal Footage of All Units calculates the lineal footage of all the units in the job, Square foots would do the
,**same except return a square footage amount Cubic would follow accordingly.

,**Total Area of Doors would calculate the Square Footage of Doors and Drawer Fronts
,**Lineal Footage of Panels calculates the footage of Panels only,
,**
,**Type in a price to multiply the selected length by, set to zero for no effect.

,**
,**The last pair deals with the number, quantity of things.
,**Total Number of Units, is the self explanatory, everything on the job.
,**Total Number of Cabinets includes just cabinets no panels or other units
,**Total Number of Base Cabinets, Wall and Tall Cabinets are again self explanatory.
,**Then there are Panels, Base, Top and Tall.
,**Followed by the Total Number of Doors which includes Drawer Fronts, Total Number of Drawer Boxes and Total
,**Number of Pullouts.
,**
,**Set a price for the selected total to be multiplied by. Set to zero for no effect.
,**
,**The last question is a flat cost. Whatever you type in gets added to (or subtracted from) the subtotal
,**
,**All 3 of these pairs, plus the flate cost are added together to come up with a subtotal that is then added to the
,**cost of the job. You can set the price of anyone of the pairs or flat cost to zero and it will have no affect in the
,**calculation of the subtotal.


,**

